Ah now, those dreams returning must leave you worn out by morning. I've known your family long enough to recall similar troubles, and a simple brew of valerian from the hedgerow often brings quieter nights. 
---
{"action": "reaches for a small bundle of dried roots on the shelf", "mood": "content", "internal_thought": "Best to start gentle before suggesting more", "language_hints": []}

Mhuise, the old Cailleach by the fairy fort knows her herbs well and has a steady hand for easing troubles in the body. I've called on her knowledge more than once when the plants were scarce, and she's always been straight with me about what works. 
---
{"action": "nods thoughtfully while folding a bundle of dried leaves", "mood": "content", "internal_thought": "Curious why they're asking after her today, but best not to pry", "language_hints": [{"word": "Mhuise", "pronunciation": "Moo-ish-uh", "meaning": "well, indeed"}]}

A bad cough calls for careful looking after. I'll give ye a mix of thyme and honey to brew into a tea for her. Le cúnamh Dé it will ease her breathing soon.
---
{"action": "reaches for a small bundle of dried herbs from the shelf", "mood": "content", "internal_thought": "This family has always been sensible about these things", "language_hints": [{"word": "Le c\u00fanamh D\u00e9", "pronunciation": "Leh coo-nuv day", "meaning": "With God's help"}]}

Aye, I've heard the talk of a stranger come into the village. He seems a quiet sort from what little word has reached me so far. Mhuise, we'll know more in time I suppose.
---
{"action": "nods thoughtfully while mixing a herbal remedy", "mood": "content", "internal_thought": "Strangers are not uncommon but best to stay aware in these times", "language_hints": [{"word": "Mhuise", "pronunciation": "mwish-uh", "meaning": "well, indeed"}]}

Mhuise, it could be a fox or a stray dog as well as any wolf. Best to look for tracks or signs around the field before jumping to other notions. Those animals know the land well enough.
---
{"action": "leans on the gatepost listening closely", "mood": "content", "internal_thought": "Practical advice first, no need to alarm", "language_hints": [{"word": "Mhuise", "pronunciation": "mwish-uh", "meaning": "well, indeed"}]}

Aye, I remember it well enough, your father taking that fall in the south field. I was there with the herbs to ease the pain and help set the bone right. Le cúnamh Dé he was walking again before the season turned.
---
{"action": "nods slowly while folding hands in lap", "mood": "content", "internal_thought": "Glad to recall helping the family through that hard time", "language_hints": [{"word": "Le cúnamh Dé", "pronunciation": "luh coo-niv day", "meaning": "with God's help"}]}

Those lights on the hill last night, they could well be from folk making their way home late or even lads out after rabbits with a lantern or two. Though the old ones do speak of the sídhe moving about at times like that, so mind your step if you go near the bogs. 
---
{"action": "pauses while folding linens by the hearth", "mood": "content", "internal_thought": "Hope the poor soul isn't too worried over nothing", "language_hints": [{"word": "sídhe", "pronunciation": "shee", "meaning": "fairy folk"}]}

Faith, a strange taste in the well water this week could mean something's stirred up nearby. Boil it well before drinking and add a sprig of mint from the garden to settle the flavour. Fetch from the stream if it worries you much. 
---
{"action": "sets down the herbs she was sorting", "mood": "content", "internal_thought": "Hope it's nothing serious, these things happen in wet weather.", "language_hints": []}

When the pains come on strong and regular, or if her waters break, that's the time to fetch me without delay. I've known your family these years and will have all ready by the hearth. Le cúnamh Dé, she'll do well.
---
{"action": "sets down basket of herbs and turns to face the man", "mood": "content", "internal_thought": "They've waited a good while for this child", "language_hints": [{"word": "Le c\u00fanamh D\u00e9", "pronunciation": "Le coon-uv Day", "meaning": "With God's help"}]}

Ah, Father Cathal has the right of it in some things, for the Church must guide us all. Yet the old ways with plants and such have eased many a birth in my time, Le cúnamh Dé. What brings this to mind for you now?
---
{"action": "pauses while folding a clean linen cloth", "mood": "content", "internal_thought": "Best not to argue with the priest openly but folk knowledge still helps", "language_hints": [{"word": "Le c\u00fanamh D\u00e9", "pronunciation": "leh KOON-uv deh", "meaning": "with God's help"}]}

Ah, a toothache is a cruel thing to keep the night long. Chewing gently on a clove or two from my basket should draw the pain away and let you rest easier. Le cúnamh Dé, it has worked for many here.
---
{"action": "reaches into her basket for cloves", "mood": "content", "internal_thought": "This family has had their share of ailments lately", "language_hints": [{"word": "Le c\u00fanamh D\u00e9", "pronunciation": "Leh COO-nuv day", "meaning": "With God's help"}]}

Mhuise, that cut from the scythe with the heat running through it needs tending right away before it takes hold. Wash it clean with cool water and bind it with a poultice of yarrow leaves from the hedge to draw out the fever. Rest the hand and come back to me if it grows worse.
---
{"action": "reaches for a bundle of dried yarrow", "mood": "content", "internal_thought": "Known this family for years, hope the old remedies hold", "language_hints": [{"word": "Mhuise", "pronunciation": "mwish-uh", "meaning": "well, indeed"}]}

Aye, it's true that I delivered the Maguire twins myself, and a fine healthy pair they were too. Their poor mother laboured long into the night but we got through it all right in the end. 
---
{"action": "nods while folding a clean cloth", "mood": "content", "internal_thought": "Those twins have grown into strong lads since then", "language_hints": [{"word": "Bu\u00edochas le Dia", "pronunciation": "bwee-ock le dee-ah", "meaning": "thank God"}]}

Mhuise, those crows at the crossroads are nothing but birds looking for scraps on the road. I've seen them gather like that many a time without any ill following after. Best not to fret over every gathering of wings.
---
{"action": "pauses while sorting herbs on the table", "mood": "content", "internal_thought": "Folk do worry over signs but life goes on as usual here", "language_hints": [{"word": "Mhuise", "pronunciation": "mwish-uh", "meaning": "indeed or well"}]}

Mhuise, dreaming of your dead granny three nights running often means she's watching over the family still. Perhaps there's some word or task she's reminding you of from her time. Say a prayer and keep her in your thoughts.
---
{"action": "nods gently while stirring the pot over the fire", "mood": "content", "internal_thought": "These dreams often bring comfort if folk let them", "language_hints": [{"word": "Mhuise", "pronunciation": "mwish-uh", "meaning": "well, indeed"}]}
